      "content": "but that's just more work. more \"messy\" stuff to deal with. i've spent my whole life trying to rebuild, and i'm just... empty. there's no more energy to fix the \"machinery.\" if something is just fundamentally defective, at what point is it more logical to just accept it? like, isn't there a point where just stopping the struggle is more realistic than pretending there's something worth saving?",
